msgid "For more details please look into :option:`pio project init --board`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_ci.rst:95
msgid ""
"Path to directory where PlatformIO will initialise new project. By default "
"it's temporary directory within your operating system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_ci.rst:100
msgid ""
"This directory will be removed at the end of build process. If you want to "
"keep it, please use :option:`pio ci --keep-build-dir`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_ci.rst:106
msgid "Don't remove :option:`pio ci --build-dir` after build process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_ci.rst:111
msgid "Build project using pre-configured :ref:`projectconf`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_ci.rst:116
msgid ""
"Pass additional options from :ref:`projectconf` to :ref:`cmd_project_init` "
"command. For example, automatically install dependent libraries ``pio ci --"
"project-option=\"lib_deps=ArduinoJSON\"`` or ignore specific library ``pio "
"ci --project-option=\"lib_ignore=SomeLib\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_ci.rst:122
msgid ""
"Use multiple ``--project-option`` to pass multiple options to :ref:"
"`projectconf`. One option per one argument. For example, ``pio ci --project-"
"option=\"build_unflags = -std=gnu++11\" --project-option=\"build_flags = -"
"std=c++14\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_ci.rst:129
msgid ""
"Process specified environments declared in :option:`pio ci --project-conf`. "
"Multiple environments are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_ci.rst:135
msgid "Shows detailed information when processing environments."
